# Add E2E integration test for full crawl → sync → summarize → sheet-verify pipeline

## Context

No end-to-end test exists that exercises the entire pipeline from crawl through Google Sheets verification. Each package has unit tests but there is no cross-package flow test that:
1. Runs `fci-crawl`
2. Runs `fci-sync`
3. Runs `fci-summarize`
4. Verifies every column in the resulting Google Sheet

This test also serves as the **master validation** for all other issues in this batch — they cannot all be considered resolved until this E2E test passes.

### Files to create
- `packages/cli/tests/e2e-full.test.ts` — Full pipeline integration test

The test should use Vitest, run against the real standredekamouraska urbanisme URL, and validate every column in the final Google Sheet output.

---

## E2E Test

**This IS the issue.** The issue is resolved only when this test passes.

```bash
rm -rf /tmp/fci-full-e2e

# Full pipeline run
echo "=== Crawl ==="
node packages/crawler/dist/cli.js \
  --url "https://www.standredekamouraska.ca/espace-citoyen/urbanisme/" \
  --output /tmp/fci-full-e2e

echo "=== Sync ==="
node packages/gws-sync/dist/cli.js \
  --inventory /tmp/fci-full-e2e/_inventory.csv \
  --drive-folder "1al1jC0VIkQvbWL_t_jaXLZrkrSObpnbl" \
  --client "e2e-test" \
  --project "full-pipeline"

echo "=== Summarize ==="
node packages/ai-summarizer/dist/cli.js \
  --inventory /tmp/fci-full-e2e/_inventory.csv \
  --concurrency 1 \
  --provider "opencode-go" \
  --model "minimax-m2.5"

echo "=== Re-Sync (push AI results to Sheet) ==="
node packages/gws-sync/dist/cli.js \
  --inventory /tmp/fci-full-e2e/_inventory.csv \
  --drive-folder "1al1jC0VIkQvbWL_t_jaXLZrkrSObpnbl" \
  --client "e2e-test" \
  --project "full-pipeline"

# Validate ALL columns in _public_schema.csv (the CSV used for sheet upload)
node --input-type=module << 'TEST'
import { readFileSync } from 'fs';
import { execSync } from 'child_process';

// Find the public schema CSV
let csvPath = '/tmp/fci-full-e2e/_public_schema.csv';
try { readFileSync(csvPath); } catch {
  const found = execSync('find /tmp/fci-full-e2e -name "*.csv" 2>/dev/null').toString().trim();
  csvPath = found.split('\n').filter(f => f.includes('public'))[0] || csvPath;
}

const content = readFileSync(csvPath, 'utf8');
const lines = content.split('\n').filter(l => l.trim());
const headerLine = lines[0];
const dataLine = lines[1];

const parseLine = (line) => {
  const fields = [], cur = [];
  let inQuotes = false;
  for (let i = 0; i < line.length; i++) {
    const c = line[i];
    if (inQuotes) {
      if (c === '"') {
        if (line[i+1] === '"') { cur.push('"'); i++; }
        else { inQuotes = false; fields.push(cur.join('')); cur.length = 0; }
      } else { cur.push(c); }
    } else {
      if (c === '"') inQuotes = true;
      else if (c === ',') { fields.push(cur.join('')); cur.length = 0; }
      else { cur.push(c); }
    }
  }
  fields.push(cur.join(''));
  return fields;
};

const cols = parseLine(headerLine);
const vals = parseLine(dataLine);
const get = (col) => { const i = cols.indexOf(col); return i >= 0 ? vals[i] : ''; };

const requiredCols = [
  'URL', 'Titre', 'Description', 'Resume_200_chars', 'Type_de_page',
  'Profondeur_URL', 'Nb_mots', 'Statut_HTTP', 'Langue', 'Date_modifiee',
  'Canonical', 'Noindex', 'Nb_images', 'Fichiers_liés',
  'Lien_Google_Doc', 'Lien_dossier_Drive'
];

const results = requiredCols.map(col => {
  const v = get(col);
  const ok = v && v.length > 0;
  console.log(ok ? '✅' : '❌', col, ':', JSON.stringify(v.slice(0, 80)));
  return ok;
});

if (results.every(Boolean)) {
  console.log('\n🎉 ALL 16 SHEET COLUMNS POPULATED — FULL PIPELINE E2E TEST PASSED');
} else {
  console.log('\n❌ FAILURES:', requiredCols.filter((_, i) => !results[i]).join(', '));
  process.exit(1);
}
TEST
```

All 16 columns must be non-empty. The issue is resolved only when this test passes. This test also validates that Issues #1, #2, and #3 are all properly fixed.

